<%# The site mark: the kamal (كمال) — a star-measuring instrument used by Arab navigators, a square tile plus a cord threaded through the center
    and tied with a knot, used to measure star altitude and fix latitude. This panel does the same thing: it does not steer, it only keeps
    taking readings so you know where you are. The cord and knot are the only brand gold site-wide.

    It must be inlined into the page rather than written as <img src>: the colors go through the --mark-* custom properties,
    dark mode works by reassigning those variables, and an SVG inside an <img> cannot reach the page's variables.

    The favicon is a separate copy: public/icon.svg. It lives in the tab bar and likewise cannot get the page variables,
    so that copy carries literal values and its own prefers-color-scheme media query.
    If you change the shape here, remember to change that copy in sync.

    locals:
      size     any CSS length
      reading  optional; when true, the knot slides up and down the cord — used while collecting (see .mark--reading).
               The animation acts only on the two gold parts and the tile stays still: the cord and knot do the reading, and the tile is the reference. %>
<% reading = local_assigns.fetch(:reading, false) %>
<svg class="mark<%= " mark--reading" if reading %>"
     style="width: <%= size %>; height: <%= size %>"
     viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="img" aria-label="Kamal Panel" focusable="false"
     xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <rect width="24" height="24" rx="6" fill="var(--mark-tile)"/>
  <%# the tile %>
  <rect x="3.4" y="5.2" width="17.2" height="7.2" rx="2.2" fill="var(--mark-on)"/>
  <%# The hole where the cord passes through the center of the tile. At 16px it disappears, which is acceptable — it is a detail that
      only needs to hold once enlarged, not a part that recognition depends on. %>
  <circle cx="12" cy="8.8" r="1.25" fill="var(--mark-tile)"/>
  <%# the cord and knot %>
  <rect x="10.75" y="12.4" width="2.5" height="7.6" rx="1.25" fill="var(--mark-gold)"/>
  <g class="mark-knot">
    <circle cx="12" cy="16.6" r="2.7" fill="var(--mark-gold)"/>
    <circle cx="12" cy="16.6" r="1.05" fill="var(--mark-tile)"/>
  </g>
</svg>
